Skjermbilde-2026-06-23-kl.-13.08.42.png 1x"/&gt;&lt;img alt="Skjermbilde 2026-06-23 kl. 13.08.42.png" loading="lazy" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7"/&gt;&lt;/picture&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="list_item list_item_frontpage_16_9 item"&gt;&lt;div class="card_details"&gt;&lt;div class="component_primary_tag"&gt;Articles&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="component_secondary_tag"&gt; New research &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="card_item"&gt;&lt;svg aria-hidden="true" fill="none" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path d="M3 6H21V21H3V6Z" stroke="#222222"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;path d="M3 11L21 11" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;path d="M9 16H15" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="square"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;path d="M8 3L8 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;path d="M16 3L16 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;time datetime="2026-06-11"&gt;June 11, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="main_content"&gt;&lt;div class="left_container"&gt;&lt;h2 class="list_title"&gt;&lt;a href="/en/news/why-ai-and-automation-do-not-equal-better-security" title="Why AI and Automation Do Not Equal Better Security"&gt;Why AI and Automation Do Not Equal Better Security&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p class="abstract"&gt; AI and machine learning are widely assumed to deliver better cybersecurity. But human experience and judgement remain deeply embedded in detecting and countering digital threats, according to a new article. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a aria-hidden="" class="image_container" href="/en/news/why-ai-and-automation-do-not-equal-better-security" tabindex="-1" title="Why AI and Automation Do Not Equal Better Security"&gt;&lt;figure class=""&gt;&lt;picture&gt;&lt;source srcset="https://www.nupi.no/var/nupi/storage/images/_aliases/scaledown210_180/8/0/6/3/126